  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "He-W 882.04 Four Month Extended Medical Assistance Due to New or Increased Spousal Support. Pursuant to 42 CFR 435.115, as amended, and 42 USC 1396u-1(c)(1), medical assistance shall be extended for 4 additional months when the primary reason for the termination of categorically needy medical assistance is increased income which was caused in whole or in part by new or increased spousal support income.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1 at Chapter Heading He-W 600) #5171, eff 6-26-91; ss by #6531, INTERIM, eff 6-27-97, EXPIRES: 10-25-97; ss by #6614, eff 10-24-97; ss by #7328, eff 8-1-00; ss by #9207, eff 7-19-08; ss by #11169, eff 8-26-16 (See Revision Note at Part heading for He-W 882)",
